--TEST--
A keyed `foreach` over a `Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>` written with `var` on both sides hides two types, and each gets its hint after its name: the map's key type and its value type, `rule:types/var-inference` and `rule:iteration/keyed-interfaces`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Tag {
    public string $name = "red";
}
var $weights = new Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>();
foreach ($weights as var $tag => var $n) {
    echo $n;
}
--REQUEST--
inlayHint
--EXPECT--
5:13 type : Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>
6:30 type : Tag
6:40 type : int
